 : ConditionallyCompleteLinearOrder.{u} α] [inst_1 : TopologicalSpace.{u} α] [OrderTopology.{u} α]\n  [DenselyOrdered.{u} α] {a b : α} {s : Set.{u} α},\n  IsClosed.{u} (Inter.inter.{u} s (Set.Icc.{u} a b)) →\n    Membership.mem.{u, u} s a →\n      (∀ (x : α),\n          Membership.mem.{u, u} (Inter.inter.{u} s (Set.Ico.{u} a b)) x →\n            Membership.mem.{u, u} (nhdsWithin.{u} x (Set.Ioi.{u} x)) s) →\n        HasSubset.Subset.{u} (Set.Icc.{u} a b) s","unsafe":false,"value":288,"source":{"code":"/-- A \"continuous induction principle\" for a closed interval: if a set `s` meets `[a, b]`\non a closed subset, contains `a`, and for any `x ∈ s ∩ [a, b)` the set `s` includes some open\nneighborhood of `x` within `(x, +∞)`, then `[a, b] ⊆ s`. -/\ntheorem IsClosed.Icc_subset_of_forall_mem_nhdsWithin {a b : α} {s : Set α}\n    (hs : IsClosed (s ∩ Icc a b)) (ha : a ∈ s) (hgt : ∀ x ∈ s ∩ Ico a b, s ∈ 𝓝[>] x) :\n    Icc a b ⊆ s :=\n  hs.Icc_subset_of_forall_mem_nhdsGT_of_Icc_subset ha\n    (fun _t ht h't ↦ hgt _ ⟨h't ⟨ht.1, le_rfl⟩, ht⟩)","start":393,"end":400},"axioms":["Classical.choice","Quot.sound","propext"]}